{"kind":"request","text":"Concrete G2 query design after G0b. Propose queryItems(reader,{v:1,type,states:[sorted unique declared names],ids?:[sorted unique IDs]},cursor?) with up to16states/100IDs, ascendingID, row100 + byte256KiB page caps and explicit totalcandidate/work bound. New opaque canonical-base64 cursor binds full incarnation/head,query digest/order/last ID; head drift yields named stale-cursor restart/refusal, never mixes heads. Cursor is routing/continuation, not authority or a prefix-integrity proof. Authenticate before exposing state/head/cursor errors. One oversized item refuses whole rather than skipping; if next legal item exceeds remaining page bytes, return continuation at last emittedID. SQL reuse item_by_state with per-state bounded candidate reads/ID merge, not whole live Summary or all-item arrays. Inspect native plan and size-before-materialization primitive; do not accept a LIMIT that still sorts/scans unbounded source rows. Proposed bounded row-size metadata read (exact SQLite primitive/version must be verified) then only admitted item bodies read; if unavailable, supply safe schema/migration decision instead of loading huge rows first. Signed resource argument = fixed-width tagged digest of exact versioned query + cursor + fixed bounds/order. Add explicit SignedReadName query-items. Authority choice needs decision: normal session/full reader keeps existing summary+final-item visibility. Limited/signed bootstrap query should supply only declared LIVE states under the same scoped eligibility as existing summary; final-state query remains forbidden because existing signed items name is unsupported. Do not turn causal-history eligibility or register whole-history privilege into arbitrary item-state authority. For query signed admission, require current summary-equivalent local/genesis-root eligibility before head/query disclosure. Recheck normal freshness/incarnation on every page. Is this precise initial policy acceptable, or should signed query wait for a separate current-membership authority contract? Then client consumers must explicitly follow continuation and restart/refuse on head drift, not silently collect all arrays. No source started for this slice.","body":{"conditions":"Pre-Source bounded query/authentication design decision only. No Source approval. Preserve existing authority and head-drift refusal, bounded indexed work/bytes and independently delivered paged consumers; full e029 remains owed.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"4817b532e7a1a118634cb7947b05f7d5d16f726c9d30ea22ff7eaf7db3634e80"}}